1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,820
Last time, we designed a school bag, like engineers.

2
00:00:04,110 --> 00:00:05,360
Fabric straps.

3
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:06,660
A metal zip.

4
00:00:06,980 --> 00:00:08,270
A plastic base.

5
00:00:08,510 --> 00:00:10,180
But will the new strap hold?

6
00:00:13,435 --> 00:00:14,665
Lock in first.

7
00:00:14,935 --> 00:00:17,335
A little frog is hiding in this video.

8
00:00:17,615 --> 00:00:18,815
Can you spot it?

9
00:00:19,393 --> 00:00:20,693
Today you'll learn:

10
00:00:20,897 --> 00:00:22,257
Test your design.

11
00:00:22,457 --> 00:00:23,937
Design a zoo home.

12
00:00:24,135 --> 00:00:25,895
Keep the great variety.

13
00:00:27,578 --> 00:00:28,458
Round one.

14
00:00:28,768 --> 00:00:30,738
The old strap held five weights.

15
00:00:31,048 --> 00:00:32,038
Then it tore.

16
00:00:32,338 --> 00:00:34,148
How many will the new strap hold?

17
00:00:34,438 --> 00:00:36,038
One, fewer than five.

18
00:00:36,308 --> 00:00:37,338
Two, five.

19
00:00:37,618 --> 00:00:39,108
Three, more than five.

20
00:00:39,388 --> 00:00:40,878
Show me with your fingers.

21
00:00:47,344 --> 00:00:48,324
Locked in!

22
00:00:48,452 --> 00:00:49,272
Two!

23
00:00:49,312 --> 00:00:50,772
A strap is a strap!

24
00:00:50,818 --> 00:00:51,558
Three!

25
00:00:51,618 --> 00:00:52,788
Thicker fabric!

26
00:00:52,841 --> 00:00:53,381
Three.

27
00:00:54,705 --> 00:00:55,855
Look closer.

28
00:00:56,445 --> 00:00:59,115
Same length, same width: a fair test.

29
00:00:59,534 --> 00:01:00,204
One.

30
00:01:00,484 --> 00:01:01,124
Two.

31
00:01:01,284 --> 00:01:02,104
Three.

32
00:01:02,244 --> 00:01:03,004
Four.

33
00:01:03,154 --> 00:01:03,994
Five.

34
00:01:04,114 --> 00:01:05,824
The old strap tore here.

35
00:01:06,237 --> 00:01:06,967
Six.

36
00:01:07,247 --> 00:01:07,967
Seven.

37
00:01:08,157 --> 00:01:08,877
Eight.

38
00:01:09,017 --> 00:01:09,837
Nine!

39
00:01:09,987 --> 00:01:10,977
No tear.

40
00:01:11,287 --> 00:01:13,257
The new strap holds more weights.

41
00:01:13,837 --> 00:01:14,967
It is stronger.

42
00:01:15,567 --> 00:01:16,607
Now we know!

43
00:01:16,822 --> 00:01:20,662
After designing, engineers test their product.

44
00:01:24,067 --> 00:01:25,427
The answer is three.

45
00:01:25,707 --> 00:01:26,877
More than five!

46
00:01:27,167 --> 00:01:28,237
Three fingers?

47
00:01:28,507 --> 00:01:29,717
One finger up!

48
00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:31,260
Be the new strap!

49
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:32,560
Shrink down.

50
00:01:32,810 --> 00:01:33,770
Quietly.

51
00:01:36,051 --> 00:01:38,791
You are the new strap, hanging from the stand.

52
00:01:39,451 --> 00:01:41,011
A weight pulls you down.

53
00:01:41,811 --> 00:01:42,751
Then another.

54
00:01:43,561 --> 00:01:44,961
You are pulled tight.

55
00:01:45,626 --> 00:01:46,356
Six.

56
00:01:46,986 --> 00:01:47,706
Seven.

57
00:01:48,246 --> 00:01:48,966
Eight.

58
00:01:49,456 --> 00:01:50,276
Nine!

59
00:01:50,756 --> 00:01:51,906
You do not tear.

60
00:01:52,406 --> 00:01:53,486
You are strong!

61
00:01:55,716 --> 00:01:57,716
Now, the same plan, for a zoo!

62
00:01:57,996 --> 00:01:59,723
Design a home for the goats.

63
00:01:59,743 --> 00:02:00,853
What is it for?

64
00:02:01,123 --> 00:02:04,203
To keep the goats safe, and to let visitors see them.

65
00:02:07,454 --> 00:02:08,584
Look closer.

66
00:02:09,194 --> 00:02:10,864
A goat home, at the zoo.

67
00:02:12,074 --> 00:02:14,084
A goat pushes the wooden fence.

68
00:02:14,664 --> 00:02:15,664
No break.

69
00:02:16,294 --> 00:02:17,464
Wood is strong.

70
00:02:18,874 --> 00:02:21,384
Between the rails, we can see the goats.

71
00:02:25,510 --> 00:02:26,500
Not glass!

72
00:02:26,550 --> 00:02:28,170
A goat's knock could break it!

73
00:02:28,596 --> 00:02:29,756
Say it with me!

74
00:02:30,464 --> 00:02:33,624
The physical properties of a material allow it to be used in

75
00:02:33,644 --> 00:02:34,784
certain ways.

76
00:02:35,444 --> 00:02:39,424
It is important to choose a material whose physical property is suitable

77
00:02:39,444 --> 00:02:41,964
for the intended use of the object.

78
00:02:45,592 --> 00:02:49,342
A zoo puts its animals in groups, so visitors can learn their

79
00:02:49,362 --> 00:02:51,252
similarities and differences.

80
00:02:51,312 --> 00:02:52,272
My zoo map!

81
00:02:52,412 --> 00:02:53,412
One: fish.

82
00:02:53,452 --> 00:02:54,702
Goldfish and koi.

83
00:02:54,822 --> 00:02:55,822
Two: birds.

84
00:02:55,902 --> 00:02:57,822
Flamingo, macaw and dragonfly.

85
00:02:57,992 --> 00:02:59,282
Three: amphibians.

86
00:02:59,312 --> 00:03:00,732
Frog and salamander.

87
00:03:01,012 --> 00:03:01,912
Showdown!

88
00:03:02,222 --> 00:03:03,352
Double points.

89
00:03:03,622 --> 00:03:05,242
One line has a mistake.

90
00:03:05,532 --> 00:03:07,292
Line one, two, or three?

91
00:03:07,592 --> 00:03:09,062
Show me with your fingers.

92
00:03:15,537 --> 00:03:16,517
Locked in!

93
00:03:16,645 --> 00:03:19,765
Two. A dragonfly has six legs.

94
00:03:19,935 --> 00:03:21,475
It is an insect!

95
00:03:21,528 --> 00:03:22,308
Two!

96
00:03:22,388 --> 00:03:23,788
Birds have feathers.

97
00:03:23,858 --> 00:03:25,608
A dragonfly has none!

98
00:03:27,039 --> 00:03:28,079
Two fingers?

99
00:03:28,319 --> 00:03:30,249
Put up two more on your score hand!

100
00:03:30,447 --> 00:03:31,187
Oops.

101
00:03:31,237 --> 00:03:32,547
The wings fooled me!

102
00:03:33,199 --> 00:03:34,279
Six groups.

103
00:03:34,579 --> 00:03:36,349
So many kinds of living things!

104
00:03:36,629 --> 00:03:37,969
A great variety.

105
00:03:38,024 --> 00:03:40,964
Why is it important to maintain diversity?

106
00:03:42,574 --> 00:03:43,864
Say it with me!

107
00:03:44,579 --> 00:03:48,229
Living things that are not able to survive will become extinct.

108
00:03:48,729 --> 00:03:50,929
This means that they will all die out.

109
00:03:53,940 --> 00:03:55,830
So we take care of every kind.

110
00:03:56,392 --> 00:03:57,497
Say it with us!

111
00:03:58,157 --> 00:03:59,147
Design it!

112
00:03:59,737 --> 00:04:01,006
Part by part!

113
00:04:04,557 --> 00:04:05,505
Choose it!

114
00:04:06,137 --> 00:04:07,617
A suitable material!

115
00:04:10,957 --> 00:04:11,919
Test it!

116
00:04:12,537 --> 00:04:13,572
Then you know!

117
00:04:18,112 --> 00:04:19,582
Show me your score hand!

118
00:04:19,862 --> 00:04:20,912
More than one?

119
00:04:21,212 --> 00:04:22,572
You beat the Buddies.

120
00:04:22,872 --> 00:04:23,932
Three fingers?

121
00:04:24,202 --> 00:04:25,212
High five!

122
00:04:25,717 --> 00:04:27,107
Did you spot the frog?

123
00:04:27,417 --> 00:04:29,427
It was on the lily pad in the pond!

124
00:04:29,717 --> 00:04:31,017
Tell someone at home.

125
00:04:31,804 --> 00:04:33,334
Next time: the Sun!

126
00:04:33,644 --> 00:04:35,204
Every evening, it goes.

127
00:04:35,484 --> 00:04:37,354
Every morning, it comes back.

128
00:04:37,634 --> 00:04:38,314
Why?

129
00:04:38,624 --> 00:04:40,394
One, the Sun moves away.

130
00:04:40,664 --> 00:04:42,084
Two, the Earth turns.

131
00:04:42,354 --> 00:04:44,184
Three, clouds hide the Sun.

132
00:04:44,454 --> 00:04:45,774
Lock in your answer!

133
00:04:45,826 --> 00:04:46,346
Easy!

134
00:04:46,666 --> 00:04:48,396
The Sun needs a nap, like me!

135
00:04:49,122 --> 00:04:51,322
Let's read today's key words together!

136
00:04:51,612 --> 00:04:52,372
Ready?

137
00:04:52,659 --> 00:04:53,429
Test.

138
00:04:54,692 --> 00:04:55,682
Diversity.

139
00:04:57,229 --> 00:04:58,169
Extinct.

140
00:04:59,620 --> 00:05:00,560
Well done!

141
00:05:01,542 --> 00:05:02,643
Say it with us!

142
00:05:03,443 --> 00:05:04,193
Ready?

143
00:05:04,317 --> 00:05:04,977
One!

144
00:05:05,317 --> 00:05:06,017
two!

145
00:05:06,322 --> 00:05:07,497
Now you know!
